8	 * of this project's own agents, 202 tool calls: 37 of the 63 shell calls were
9	 * `sed -n A,Bp` and `grep -rn`, the agent rebuilding both by hand. The reviewer,
10	 * which has no shell, could not — it read one 1,700-line file four times with `head`
11	 * and `tail`, which never reach the middle, and 43% of everything it read came back
12	 * truncated.
13	 *
14	 * Candidates with the missing capabilities were evaluated by starting them and reading
15	 * their real schemas, because the documentation was wrong about the official one. None
16	 * was both mature and complete: the server that is official lacks the primitives, and
17	 * the ones that have them are single-author projects, one without a licence. Adopting
18	 * any would also have meant 14 to 17 tools where six will do, with names and truncation
19	 * messages belonging to somebody else.
20	 *
21	 * ## The names
22	 *
23	 * `read`, `grep`, `glob`, `edit`, `write`, `list` — what OpenCode and Claude Code call
24	 * them, which is what a model has seen most. They arrive unprefixed because this server
25	 * sets `unprefixed: true`; see `ToolDef::unprefixed` in the core for why two servers
26	 * cannot both claim a name and what happens when they try.
27	 *
28	 * ## The rule every result here follows
29	 *
30	 * A result that left something out says what to ask for to get the rest. A truncation
31	 * that stops mid-file with no next step is what produced four reads of one file: the
32	 * agent changed `head: 40` to `head: 760` because nothing told it that the number it
